{
  "info": {
    "name": "AI-Powered Job Application Tailoring Platform",
    "description": "Requests for every live API endpoint of this project, against the currently staged backend (us-east-1). Endpoint reference: API.md.\n\nSuggested order (run the requests top-to-bottom in a folder):\n  1. Profile folder  - parse free text, save the profile, read it back\n  2. Job descriptions folder - save a job, read it back, list them (the save response stores job_id automatically)\n  3. Tailoring folder - keyword preview, then full Bedrock generation (both saved-job and ad-hoc paths)\n\nNotes:\n- profile-service: PUT /profile is an upsert keyed by email; project/experience embeddings are cached and reused if the text is unchanged, and education entries are stored as-is (never embedded or matched).\n- job-service: PUT /job-description always creates a brand-new item (fresh UUID every call - no dedup), normalizes email, and embeds raw_description at save time.\n- tailoring-service: /tailor-preview is keyword-only and free (no Bedrock). /tailor-generate is pure-embedding matching + a Claude Haiku 4.5 call. Both need a saved profile; /tailor-generate also accepts an ad-hoc job body that is never persisted.\n- The /cv/* endpoints from the old cv-service were removed from the deployed stack and are intentionally not included.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "base_url",
      "value": "https://qmpqjnqmn8.execute-api.us-east-1.amazonaws.com"
    },
    {
      "key": "email",
      "value": "alex.morgan@example.com"
    },
    {
      "key": "job_id",
      "value": ""
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Profile",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "POST /profile/parse - free text to profile schema",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('has a profile key', () => {",
                  "  const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(json).to.have.property('profile');",
                  "  pm.expect(json.profile).to.have.property('full_name');",
                  "  pm.expect(json.profile).to.have.property('experience');",
                  "  pm.expect(json.profile).to.have.property('education');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n    \"raw_text\": \"Backend-focused software engineer with about 4 years at Nimbus Software (2021-2024), where I built Python services on AWS and worked with Postgres, Docker, and CI/CD pipelines. Before that a stint at Loopware doing React frontend work. Personal side project: Budget Tracker, a full-stack web app I built in 2023 to learn modern frontend dev. Studied Computer Science at State University 2017-2021, graduated with honors.\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/profile/parse",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["profile", "parse"]
            }
          },
          "response": []
        },
